Biography: (Persephone is the youngest of remaining Goddesses. She seems to be a naive kind girl and almost everyone treats her like that. Still, she is really smart and for her life she experienced much more than other goddesses: being Hades wife, she learned a lot about death and almost every dark and cruel things in our world. Her husband was the only person who treated her as a person, not as a child. She suffers greatly from his death);

Secret: (in the fight with Chronos Persephone lost her mother, Goddess Demeter and her husband, God Hades. Even if she tries to remain her playful and happy demeanor, she grieves about them every single day. When she is alone, she often cries thinking about her dead mother and dead husband and cries. Due to all of this losses she is feeling extremely lonely even if she's trying to hide it behind childish behaviour);
